        "original_id": "e513c11a-bc6a-523d-abfe-8d5bb5c42dac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Piet Norval, Emilio Sánchez, Wayne Ferreira\n- Events: 1988 Olympic Games, 1992 Summer Olympics, 2008 Davis Cup, 2012 wheelchair tennis events\n- Roles: doubles competitor, doubles partner, Davis Cup captain, tournament director\n\nFacts:\n- Emilio Sánchez won the men's doubles silver medal at the 1988 Olympic Games.\n- Emilio Sánchez won three Grand Slam doubles titles.\n- Piet Norval represented South Africa in the doubles competition at the 1992 Summer Olympics in Barcelona.\n- Piet Norval partnered Wayne Ferreira in the doubles competition at the 1992 Summer Olympics in Barcelona.\n- Emilio Sánchez captained Spain to Davis Cup success in 2008.\n- Emilio Sánchez was a tournament director for two wheelchair tennis events in 2012.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cbe9c8f0-9f6c-5dc3-8e1e-7729c4d50e0a",
        "text": "Page: Piet Norval. Sentence: The right-hander represented his native country in the doubles competition at the 1992 Summer Olympics in Barcelona, where he partnered Wayne Ferreira.\nPage: Emilio Sánchez. Sentence: He won three Grand Slam doubles titles and the men's doubles silver medal at the 1988 Olympic Games.\nPage: Emilio Sánchez. Sentence: Sanchez since retiring captained his nation to Davis Cup success in 2008.\nPage: Emilio Sánchez. Sentence: In 2012 Sanchez was a tournament director for two wheelchair tennis events.",
